# Theme Progression Guidance

# Intent
#:layer #!pragmatics

Suggest a light → dark rhythm to support daily cognitive cadence.
Enable future plugins to automate progression or choose themed arcs.

# Default progression (day arc)
- Morning: atelier-light
- Midday: hud-light or nebula-light
- Afternoon: nebula-dark (gentle contrast)
- Evening: atelier-dark
- Late: alcove-dark (reading + compression)

# Alternate progression (creative arc)
- Morning: nebula-light
- Midday: atelier-light
- Afternoon: atelier-dark
- Evening: alcove-dark
- Late: hud-dark

# Plugin hooks (future)
- setting: appearance.themeStage
- setting: appearance.theme
- data: data-theme-transitioning
- data: data-theme-stage

# Notes
- Progression should prefer low-motion transitions.
- Stages can stay at 0 (Functional) until user opts into personality.
- Add “residency packs” as theme bundles with curated arcs.

?["How does selector expansion compose across nested $-expressions?"]
  #:depth #!educational  // lens: collection
  $($@_ => $^[_]) => &[result.flatten]
  ~<@spw/conventions/selection.spw>
  !probe{ "expand $@biome/$^[algos] step by step; show intermediate selector states like a debugger" }

?["Is selector composition associative? Does ($a => $b) => $c equal $a => ($b => $c)?"]
  #:depth #!mathematical  // lens: formula
  ~#left_assoc: "$($@docs => $^[theory]) => $#concept"
  ~#right_assoc: "$@docs => $($^[theory] => $#concept)"
  !probe{ "enumerate cases where associativity breaks; these are the interesting compositional edges" }
